### 4.3 `src/service_routing/launchSetup.ts`
**Role:** Launch submission endpoint.

#### `launchRoutes(fastify: FastifyInstance): Promise<void>`
Fastify plugin that registers **`POST /newToken`** (mounted at `/launch/newToken`).

**Use case:** The frontend submits a token launch form with an image. The handler streams the multipart body, builds a `LaunchJobData`, enqueues it, and returns the job ID right away. The launch itself runs asynchronously.

**Inputs:**
- Header `x-user-id: string`
- Multipart file part (any one file): read into `imageBuffer` with `mimeType`. If several files are sent, the last one wins.
- Multipart fields (strings, coerced as below; defaults apply when a field is missing):

| Field | Coercion | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `name` | string | `''` | Token name |
| `symbol` | string | `''` | Token ticker |
| `description` | string | `''` | Metadata description |
| `decimals` | `Number()` | `0` | Mint decimals |
| `supply` | `Number()` | `0` | Whole-token supply (pre-decimals) |
| `revoke` | `=== 'true'` | `true`* | Revoke mint authority after minting |
| `lockMetaData` | `=== 'true'` | `true`* | Metadata immutable (`isMutable = !lockMetaData`) |
| `configAddress` | string | `''` | Meteora CP-AMM config pubkey |
| `poolPercentage` | `Number()` | `100` | % of supply deposited into the pool |
| `initialLiquiditySol` | `Number()` | `0` | SOL deposited into the pool |
| `fundingWalletId` | string | `''` | wallet-app ID of the payer/creator wallet |
| `feeWalletId` | string | `''` | wallet-app ID of the fee wallet |
| `website` / `twitter` / `telegram` | string | `''` | Socials (metadata + DB) |
| `autoBuyEnabled` | `=== 'true'` | `false` | Enable post-launch buys |
| `slaveWalletId` | string | `null` | wallet-app ID of the buyer wallet |
| `numberOfBuys` | `Number()` | `0` | Count of sequential buys |
| `solPerBuy` | `Number()` | `0` | SOL per buy |

\*A boolean field becomes `false` when it is present with any value other than the string `'true'`.

**Behavior:** `400` if no image. Otherwise `launchQueue.add("token-launch-queue", jobData)` → `202 { jobId }`. `imageBuffer` is converted with `Array.from(buffer)` so it survives JSON serialization in Redis.

